[ti:Day 20]

[00:00.00]rampant 例 Rampant inflation means that our savings will shrink a lot. 不断蔓延的通货膨胀意味着我们 的积蓄将大量缩水。
[00:07.93]caption 例 Please suggest a caption in the comments thread below. 请在下面的评论栏中写上所建议的 标题。
[00:15.33]flair 例 The single biggest factor in the success of any business, is its human capital, including the flair, talent and productivity of its workers. 任何企业要成功，唯一重要的因素就在于人力资 本，包括其员工的资质、才能和生产能力。
[00:32.30]raffle 例 To make sure your commodity investing is successful, you must adhere to the SMART strategy, that is, your goals must be speciflc, measurable, accountable, realistic and timecentric. 为确保商品投资的成功，你必须遵循 SMART 策略——你的投资目标必须清楚明确、可 量可算、动机充分、现实可行、时间可控。
[00:54.47]variation 例 There has been no variation in the price of vegetables for two months. 两个月来，蔬菜的 价格一直保持稳定。
[01:03.78]compile 例 You can compile code and run it in its default scope. 你可以编译代码，并在默认范围 内执行它。
[01:10.76]unleash 例 You might find a new way to unleash more consumer demand by boosting green consumption. 通过倡导绿色消费，我们可能会发 现一条刺激消费需求的新途径。
[01:21.84]characteristic 例 Autonomy is the characteristic of all successful institutions. 独立自治是所有成功机 构的特点。
[01:31.43]frugal 例 We should advocate a more frugal lifestyle so as to reduce the growing scale of waste pollution. 我们应该提倡一种更加节俭的生活方 式，以减小垃圾污染的增长规模。
[01:43.33]crude 例 Our store can supply the crude Coconut flbre from Thailand, the Philippines and Vietnam. 我们店供应产自泰国、菲律宾、越南等 国的天然椰棕纤维。
[01:54.42]bumpily 例 The car bounced along the mountain road bumpily. 汽车在崎岖的山路上颠簸行驶。
[02:01.13]brick-and-mortar 例 In the brick-and-mortar travel agent model, a trained agent meets with the traveller in person or establishes a relationship over the phone. 在传统的实体旅行社模式下，训练有素的 代理商会亲自与旅行者会面，或在电话上与客户 沟通。
[02:19.74]feeble 例 Tighter credit conditions are sapping already feeble demand. 紧缩的信贷让已经无力 的需求更加乏力。
[02:27.95]implication 例 The phenomenon has an interest ing implication for our company's future. 该现象对 我们公司的未来有着有趣的暗示。
[02:38.08]equality 例 We're born of equality though develop to be different. 人生来平等，尽管日后境遇各有不
[02:45.61]escort 例 Merchant ships are escorted by warships since this is the area where pirates harried. 商 船由军舰来护送，因为此海域常有海盗出没。
[02:56.42]bankruptcy 例 A great many small businesses went into bankruptcy during the financial crisis in 2008. 在2008年的金融危机中，许多小型企业都走向了 破产。
[03:08.06]gauge 例 The amount of money one makes is not the only gauge of one's success. 挣钱的多少不是衡 量一个人成功与否的唯一标准。
[03:16.54]literate 例 One of the disadvantages of the Internet is that you have to be literate to use it. 互联网的 缺点之一就是只有具备读写能力的人才能使用 它。
[03:26.95]flanker 例 Microsoft has focused more on its flankers such as the Xbox 360 to bring the Media Centre experience to the big-screen TV. 微软 已开始重点关注其延伸产品，如Xbox360，欲把 其在媒体中心方面的经验延伸到大屏幕电视上。
[03:41.86]hyperinflation 例 Hyperinflation invariably emerges in a deflationary environment of weak economic activities. 恶性通货膨胀总是出现在经济活动衰弱 的通货紧缩环境下。
[03:55.14]elasticity 例 The analysis for the market demand elasticity is very important in enterprise operations. 市场需求弹性分析对企业经营很重 要。
[04:07.19]dutiable 例 They tried to cheat the customs by not declaring dutiable goods. 他们试图通过不报应 纳税货物来蒙骗海关。
[04:15.81]uncertainty 例 Business is full of uncertainty. 商场上充满不 确定性。
[04:21.28]disparity 例 There is a growing disparity between the rich and the poor. 贫富差距愈来愈大。
[04:29.36]indulgence 例 Self-forgiveness is just another form of self indulgence. 自我宽恕只是自我放纵的另一种 表现形式。
[04:37.71]disgruntled 例 He is disgruntled at the working conditions. 他对工作条件不满意。
[04:44.55]trade-off 例 There should be a trade-off between doing the job accurately and doing it quickly. 需要在 工作的准确性和速度之间进行权衡。
[04:55.37]gratitude 例 I wish to express my gratitude to Kathy for her immense practical help with the work. 我想 向凯茜表达谢意，感谢她在工作中给了我许多实 质性的帮助。
[05:06.32]niche 例 Finding a niche market in business is the key to success. 找到业务中的利基市场是成功的 关键。
[05:13.57]enrichment 例 Life enrichment might be a result of working experience abroad. 海外工作经历可能 使人生丰富。
[05:22.47]deregulate 例 The government must deregulate access to some industries and resource prices to further the reformation. 为深化改革，政府必须撤销对某 些行业准入权和资源价格的限制。
[05:36.29]ethics 例 Confldentiality is the basic professional ethics of a lawyer. 保密是律师基本的职业道 德。
[05:44.50]enshrine 例 The memory of once being one of the workers of that company will be enshrined deep in my heart. 我会永远将在那家公司工作的
[05:56.27]illicit 例 Your company is doing something illicit. 你 的公司在做违法的事。
[06:02.16]autocratic 例 Autocratic leadership usually leads to high levels of absenteeism and staff turnover. 独裁 式领导风格往往导致高缺勤率和员工流失率。
[06:13.79]yarn 例 He spun his little brother a yarn about a policeman. 他给弟弟讲了一个警察的故事。
[06:20.36]reassure 例 He reassured us about the safety of these products. 他再次向我们保证这些产品的安全性。
[06:27.48]factor 例 This important factor was neglected by most of us. 这一重要因素被我们大多数人所忽 视。
[06:34.19]subcontract 例 To cut cost, the property developers tend to subcontract the projects to many construction contractors. 为降低成本，地产开 发商往往会将地产项目转包给许多施工承包商。
[06:48.01]foster 例 The business school has done nothing to foster accountability in students. 那家商学院在 培养学员的责任意识方面毫无作为。
[06:57.73]council 例 The matter will be brought before council this afternoon. 这件事情将在今天下午提交给委 员会讨论。
[07:05.53]collate 例 Rather than merely possessing data, we must also learn the skills necessary to acquire, collate, and evaluate information for any situation. 我们不能仅仅拥有数据，而必须学习在 任何情况下获取、整理和评估信息的必要技能。
[07:23.05]counterproductive 例 In any worst case scenario solution that FEMA might consider, the solution is not to interfere with existing farm production, as this would be counterproductive. 在任何最糟糕的情 况下，联邦紧急事务管理局所考虑的解决方案都 是不干扰现有的农业生产，因为这样做会适得其
[07:44.27]memento 例 The director gave him a photo album as a memento of his long years of service in the company. 主管送给他一本相册作为他为公司服务 多年的纪念。
[07:55.63]foolproof 例 The process is not foolproof, because markets can also be wrong. 这种方法并非万无 一失，因为市场也可能出错。
[08:04.39]career 例 Career continuity should be of great importance for the youngsters. 年轻人应注重职 业生涯的连贯性。
[08:13.28]infiltrate 例 The boss tried to inflltrate his ideas into the staff's minds. 老板设法把他的思想渗透到员工的 脑中。
[08:21.91]underbid 例 The manufacturer seems to have underbid the project by a wider margin than other competitors. 这家制造商对该项目的出价似乎比 其他同行低得多。
[08:33.95]marathon 例 Think of work as a series of sprints, not a marathon. 把工作看成多次短跑，而不是一场马 拉松。
[08:41.07]exhausted 例 An exhausted edition, whatever, fetches incredibly at auction. 只要是绝版的，不管什么 东西都能拍出天价。
[08:49.96]indent 例 With reference to your indent No. 315, we have received the relative L/C. 关于你方315号 订货单，我方已收到相关的信用证。
[08:59.27]energise 例 The first thing that we should do is to energise the administration. 我们应该做的第一 件事就是加强管理。
[09:08.31]lofty 例 All the staff of the company praised his lofty moral character. 全公司的员工都赞扬他高 尚的品德。
[09:16.38]chain 例 Sometimes the problem has already escalated up through the clients' management chain and back down to us. 有时候，问题通过 客户的管理链传到我们这里时已经升级了。
[09:29.38]embezzlement 例 Embezzlement of company funds or client funds for personal use is strictly forbidden. 因 个人使用而挪用公司或客户资金的行为是严令禁 止的。
[09:41.15]configuration 例 For better performance, you can use the computer with the better conflguration. 为了获 得更好的性能，你可以使用配置更好的电脑。
[09:52.38]consignment 例 We are faced with the problem that part of the consignment is unacceptable. 我们面临的 问题是委托运送的部分货物不被接受。
[10:02.64]booklet 例 They have designed a health education booklet for community residents. 他们为小区居 民设计了一份健康教育手册。
[10:12.09]anchor 例 He said that the government should solidly anchor inflation expectations to avoid additional volatility. 他说政府应该牢牢地控制通 货膨胀，以避免更多的波动。
